    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the AUDIT-on-create requirement for `POST /api/owners`.\n\n- **New function** `rest/function/owner/AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 takes the persisted `@Val Owner` and logs via the SLF4J logger named `AUDIT`, emitting the owner `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate`.\n- **Wired it** into `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` as a new `audit` step between `save` and `respond` (so the id is already assigned), keeping it under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbors.\n\nPlacing it after `SaveOwner` ensures `owner.getId()` is populated, and the `registrationDate`/`customerCode` logged are the same values serialized in the response \u2014 which is exactly what the test asserts (`audit.anyContains(id, customerCode, registrationDate)`).\n\nTest result: `AcceptanceTest.coreLogsAuditOnCreate` passes \u2014 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS. Observed audit line: `AUDIT - Created owner id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-10-01`.",
