    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change fits the codebase's conventions cleanly:\n\n- **Right unit.** Auditing is its own concern, so a dedicated `AuditOwnerCreated` step wired between `save` and `respond` is the idiomatic OfficeFloor shape \u2014 one small function class, one public method. Folding the log line into `SaveOwner` or `RespondWithOwnerCreated` would overload those steps; keeping it separate is correct.\n- **Placement is coherent.** It runs after `SaveOwner`, so the owner id has been assigned before it's read, and before `respond` \u2014 matching the spec (\"on successful create\").\n- **Consistent with local idiom, not just the AGENTS.md example.** I checked `SaveOwner` and the full `owners.POST.yml`: the real codebase names every step method `service` (not the descriptive names in the worked example), and puts `govern: [ transaction ]` on *every* step in this pipeline including `respond`. So `AuditOwnerCreated.service(...)` and its `govern: [ transaction ]` both match the established local pattern rather than being noise.\n- **No duplication**, and the dedicated `AUDIT` logger with id/customerCode/registrationDate matches the spec exactly.\n\nNothing to improve structurally.",
